# --- the papers themselves ---------------------------------------------------
# raw/ is publisher PDFs: large, and a git history cannot forget them. Every
# sha256 in meta/ is the claim that ties a sidecar to bytes that live only here
# and in the backup; `make verify` re-proves it.
areas/*/raw/
areas/*/inbox/
inbox/

# meta/ IS tracked, deliberately. It is small, it is the ground truth for what
# the collection holds, and a per-edit reversible diff is a far stronger audit
# trail than any ledger this project could hand-roll.
#
# outputs/ is tracked too. It holds the literature review, which IS the taxonomy;
# versioning it is the audit trail for "why did this paper's topic change between
# two builds" -- the one question add-only updates make hard to answer any other
# way. Read-only does not mean untracked.

# --- generated ---------------------------------------------------------------
areas/*/dist/
dist/
index/registry.json
dist-archive/
areas/*/data/*.npy
areas/*/data/*.npz
areas/*/data/*.pkl
areas/*/reports/build_*.txt
areas/*/reports/bib_disagreements_*.txt
# Draft reviews. make_review writes these into reports/ and installing one into
# outputs/ is what makes it the taxonomy -- so the draft is a regenerable byproduct
# that would duplicate 88 KB of outputs/ in the history on every re-clustering.
# Measurements in reports/ ARE tracked: they are the evidence for a revision.
areas/*/reports/*_literature_review.md

# library.json and similarity.json ARE tracked: they are the build's contract and
# both are deterministic, so an unchanged rebuild is a no-op for git and a dirty
# tree means the data really moved rather than that somebody ran make.

# --- the source archive this project was built from --------------------------
# Kept on disk so any claim in docs/PROVENANCE.md can be checked by diff, but it
# is 167 KB of somebody else's release and does not belong in this history.
teamlibrary-toolkit-2026-09-05/
teamlibrary-toolkit-2026-09-05.tar.gz

# --- environment -------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
